Controller SPI-NOR (SHEIPA) for RTL8197F.

The 4.14 kernel does not know the controller that is connected to the serial flash board,
therefore /proc/mtd is empty and there is nothing to mount root=/dev/mtdblock4 with.

The driver is not newly written: drivers/spi/sheipa/ files are taken from the vendor
OpenWrt of the same target rtkmipsel from which our BSP was removed, and end up in a tree
via target/linux/rtkmipsel/files/. This patch only adds wiring -
configuration symbol and assembly entry.

The driver registers the normal spi_master with transfer_one_message, so over
It runs the standard kernel stack 4.14 (MTD_SPI_NOR + MTD_M25P80). Vendor
patched m25p80 with "user mode" is intentionally not portable: it exists for the sake of
acceleration by 3.18 and overwrites the layer, which in 4.14 is moved to spi-nor.

The controller addresses (BSP_SPIC_BASE, BSP_SPIC_AUTO_BASE) are already described in bspchip.h;
the platform device registers arch/mips/rtl8197f/mtd.c.

--- a/drivers/spi/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/spi/Kconfig
@@ -527,6 +527,11 @@
 config SPI_PXA2XX_PCI
 	def_tristate SPI_PXA2XX && PCI && COMMON_CLK

+config SPI_SHEIPA
+	bool "Realtek SHEIPA SPI Controller"
+	help
+	  This is the driver for the SHEIPA SPI Controller.
+
 config SPI_ROCKCHIP
 	tristate "Rockchip SPI controller driver"
 	help
--- a/drivers/spi/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/spi/Makefile
@@ -112,3 +112,5 @@
 # SPI slave protocol handlers
 obj-$(CONFIG_SPI_SLAVE_TIME)		+= spi-slave-time.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SPI_SLAVE_SYSTEM_CONTROL)	+= spi-slave-system-control.o
+
+obj-$(CONFIG_SPI_SHEIPA)		+= sheipa/
